# SPI target, mode 0, no chip select: full duplex, one byte per frame of the
# core's coded shifter. It samples MOSI on each SCLK rise and shifts MISO out
# right after it (mode 0 only needs the next bit before the next rise). The
# lane loads each reply byte from the source stream before its first clock
# and stores each received byte; the transfer is as long as the source. The
# controller must leave at least one SCLK period between bytes (the lane
# needs about ten clocks to load the next reply).
next:   PULL                        # reply byte
        SHIFT                       # load it and start the shifter
        WAIT event:coder.word       # eighth SCLK rise
        RD readback:coder.rx_word
        PUSH
        RD readback:stream_bytes_left
        JNZ next
        HALT
